=== SIGNATURE ===
exists(arr, value)

=== COMMENT ===
Checks whether value is present anywhere in arr; returns 1 or 0.

=== CODE ===
=LAMBDA(Arr, Val, IF(ISNUMBER(XMATCH(z_scalar(Val), TOCOL(Arr), 0)), 1, 0))

=== DESCRIPTION ===
Membership test: is a value present in an array.

Arguments:
  arr   - array to search (flattened before testing).
  value - the scalar value to look for.

Single-value arguments (flags, counts, delimiters, a single lookup value) may arrive as 1x1 arrays (TOCOL(x), {x}, a one-cell FILTER/INDEX result); they are collapsed to true scalars with z_scalar, so they behave exactly like the plain value.

Returns:
  1 if value occurs in arr, otherwise 0.

Example:
  exists(list, "x")  ->  1
